; claude: networking, from scratch, for teaching: one idea per module,
; each .mli with its diagram, worked example and references, like
; physics/, audio/ and ai/ (see
; docs/claude_notes/plans/plan_dependencies_remaining.md section 2, and
; plan_networking_teaching.md for the games' part). The protocols only,
; pure OCaml, no sockets: a message is bytes in, bytes out, so the
; tests need no network and every backend, the web one included, can
; use them. The sockets are networking/unix/. A private library,
; installed as part of elm_playground.
(library
 (name networking)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries
   random ; Lehmer, Sim_net's seeded network
   crypto ; Sha1, for Websocket's handshake
   elm_core ; Base64, for it too
 )
)
